# forge-managed
#
# Files forge generates. Prettier must not rewrite them.
#
# The vue block runs `cd {{dir}} && npx prettier --write .` with
# pass_filenames: false, so `files:` decides whether the hook runs, not what it
# touches — prettier formats the whole of {{dir}}. Where a repo keeps its Vue
# app in a subdirectory that is harmless. Where the component sits at the repo
# root, prettier reaches the generated files: it reindented every `# generated:`
# marker in .pre-commit-config.yaml and requoted node-version in the CI
# workflow, and forge rewrote them back on the next sync. Two writers on one
# file have no fixed point, and the repo drifts on every run of either tool.
#
# Ownership decides, not formatting preference: these files are generated, and
# the generator is the only thing entitled to their shape.
#
# The entries name the spellings on disk across the portfolio. A release that
# changes them changes this file's settings, and a deployed copy whose settings
# do not match the template is one forge declines to adopt — so an entry swap
# lands only once every copy carries the marker above.
.pre-commit-config.yaml
.github/workflows/validate.yml
.markdownlint.json
.editorconfig
.golangci.yml
.sqlfluff
